title **Correcting a Mistake, and Who Is Allowed to See It**\nReversal semantics + row-level security

actor "Warehouse Keeper" as WH
actor "Vendor user\n<<VEN-AZAR>>" as VEN

participant "WarehouseService" as WS
database "material_movements" as TMOV
database "PostgreSQL RLS" as RLS

== The wrong quantity was booked ==

note over WH, TMOV
  PH-14-GRN-0003 recorded 120 m. The delivery note said 120,
  the truck actually carried 100. The GRN is already signed,
  already counted, already reported to the client.
end note

WH -> WS : reverse(movement GRN-0003, reason)
activate WS

WS -> WS : assert reason is not empty
WS -> TMOV : already reversed?
alt#ef4444 a reversal already points here
  TMOV --> WS : found
  WS --> WH : ValidationException\n"این تراکنش قبلا برگشت خورده است"
  note right of WS #7f1d1d
    Reversing twice would credit the
    stock back twice. A reversal is
    idempotent by refusing to repeat.
  end note
else not yet reversed
  WS -> WS : opposite = ISSUE  (for a RECEIPT)
  WS -> WS : check the reversal itself\ndoes not drive stock negative
  WS -> TMOV : INSERT PH-14-MIV-0006\ntype = ISSUE, quantity = **+120**\nreverses_movement_id = GRN-0003
end
WS --> WH : MaterialMovement
deactivate WS

WH -> WS : receive(po, qty = 100, heat "A-4471")
WS -> TMOV : INSERT PH-14-GRN-0007

note over TMOV #14532d
  **Four rows now exist, and all four stay.**
  GRN-0003 (+120) · MIV-0006 (-120) · GRN-0007 (+100)

  Balance is correct, *and* the audit trail still shows
  that somebody booked 120, noticed, and corrected it -
  with a name, a timestamp and a reason attached.

  An UPDATE would have produced the same balance and
  destroyed all of that.
end note

== The same ledger, seen by a vendor ==

VEN -> RLS : SELECT * FROM material_requisitions
activate RLS
RLS --> VEN : **0 rows**
deactivate RLS

note right of VEN #7f1d1d
  **Commercially load-bearing, not merely tidy.**

  A requisition carries the engineer's internal
  argument for *why* this material is needed and
  *how much* the project can bear. A vendor reading
  it is a vendor negotiating with your own cost
  estimate in hand.

  Unlike the punch list - where RLS mostly prevents
  noise - here a leak has a price tag.
end note

VEN -> RLS : SELECT * FROM purchase_orders
activate RLS
RLS -> RLS : USING (vendor_company_id = current tenant\nOR buyer participates in project)
RLS --> VEN : **3 rows** - only its own orders
deactivate RLS

VEN -> RLS : SELECT * FROM material_lots
RLS --> VEN : 3 rows - readable by every participant

note over RLS
  Verified live against the seeded fixture:
  | company | MRs | POs | lots |
  | VEN-AZAR (vendor)   | **0** | 3 | 3 |
  | NIOC-AFF (employer) | 3 | 3 | 3 |

  Lots and movements are readable by every project
  participant but writable only by the custodian -
  the client must be able to audit stock without
  being able to book a receipt.
end note

@enduml
